<title>MEXICO: FORECAST- Mexico 28-day Cetes to rise to 18.19 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST- Mexico 28-day Cetes to rise to 18.19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 12 basis points to 18.19 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY   CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     18.07	    18.19		   + 12 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     20.31	    20.57		   + 26 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    21.41	    21.71		   + 30 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     22.74	    22.92		   + 18 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 local (2330 GMT).</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
